  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.S.Murugesan vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety And Drug ... on 1 August, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.No.220 In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 01.08.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr. Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.No.22071 of 2024 and WMP.Nos.24049 & 24050 of 2024 M.S.Murugesan ... P Vs The Commissioner of Food Safety and Drug Administration, O/o. the Commissioner of Food Safety and Drug Administration, DMS Campus, Annasalai, Chennai 600 006 ..... Respondent Prayer : Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of Constitution praying for the issuance of a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus calli the records pertaining to the impugned order of transfer in R.No.39 2024/S12/FSD, dated 19.07.2024 on the file of the respondent and qu the same as illegal and consequently to direct the respondent to fr general transfer guidelines and then conduct the transfer counselin necessary for transfers among the Food Safety Officers in Tamilnadu within the time stipulated by this Court. For Petitioner : Mr.S.Louis For Respondent : Mrs.M.Sneha, Special Counsel for Health D 1/6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.No.2 ORDER M.S.Murugesan vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety And Drug ... Hence, the petitioner was not disturbed before three years of his tenure. M.S.Murugesan vs The Commissioner Of Food Safety And Drug ... on 1 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/16812836/ 2 6.",
    "facts": "While he was working as Sanitary Inspector cum Food Inspector at Tiruppur City Municipal Corporation, he was shifted to the newly created department called Tamil Nadu State Food Safety and Drug Administration Department in the cadre of Food Safety Officer and he was posted at Tiruppur City Municipal Corporation. On 01.07.2018, he was given transfer to Coimbatore Corporation. From then onwards, he is serving as the Food Safety Officer in Coimbatore Corporation. Now after period of nearly six years, the petitioner has been transferred from Coimbatore to Villupuram District. Therefore, the respondent strictly followed the guidelines issued as per GO.No.10 Personnel and Administrative Reforms (Per.S) Department dated 07.01.1997.",
    "arguments": "The respondent failed to frame any Rules so far for the Tamilnadu Food Safety and Drug Administration Department. Therefore, the learned counsel submitted that there should be some scheme or method to be adopted for effecting such transfers for rationalising the services of the officers."
  },
